        }
      ],
      "impact": "D10, D35, and D49 cannot light because their anodes have no positive supply path. Any status indication intended from these LEDs would be absent or behave differently from the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R71"],
      "pins": ["R71.1", "R71.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R71 is given value \"24k\" and is simulated as 24k, but its MPN and description fields specify a 24Ω part: MPN \"FRC0805J240TSD\" and description \"... 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor ...\".",
      "expected": "The schematic value, BOM MPN, and part description should agree. For this high-impedance Ethernet/common-mode clamp network, a 24k resistor is consistent with the circuit role; a 24Ω resistor would heavily load VOUTP/VOUTN and change the clamp behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R71\") (value \"24k\") (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R71 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"223\") (name \"VOUTP\") ... (node (ref \"R71\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"222\") (name \"VOUTN\") ... (node (ref \"R71\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled from the MPN/description rather than the schematic value, R71 would be 24Ω instead of 24k. That would load the Ethernet common-mode/protection node, alter the zener/MOSFET clamp biasing, and could affect Ethernet protection or signal behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.58
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist contains a clear floating LED anode net (/NET0148) that prevents D10, D35, and D49 from functioning, and R71 has a schematic/SPICE value of 24k that conflicts with its BOM MPN/description of 24Ω."
}

